Captain hold: review round 4 - decision required

Purpose
Keep the context reminder visible by stopping automatic wake turns until an explicit captain decision, preserve queued events, and continue delivering eligible terminal supervision-failure warnings once even during hold.

Captain decisions - 2026-10-06
R1-2 narrow final cleanup-window race is accepted by the captain; no coordination work, and it must not be re-raised.
Terminal failure warnings must not be hidden during hold; restore the existing once-only warning path and remove suppression and rollback.
The latest decision supersedes the earlier R2-1 suppression requirement and R3-1 ownership-patch proposal.

Round history and fixes
Round 1 found routed internal messages receiving captain reminders and late preparation-window automatic continuations.
Those approved fixes were committed in 23840ad; routed classification remains verified, and preparation checks remain intact.
Round 2 reopened the narrow final cleanup race and found consumed-but-hidden terminal warnings.
The captain accepted the narrow race; the initial warning rollback fix was committed in 51d9aa7.
Round 3 found that rollback could delete a newer failure episode's warning record.
Rather than add coordination, the captain changed the warning contract and ordered removing suppression and rollback.
That correction was committed in 63dbfa6357f177cd21ba51c120eb21249d724062.
Round 4 independently confirmed both warning findings dissolve with that correction: held terminal warnings appear once, and old cleanup no longer deletes replacement alarm records.
No new production defect was reproduced.
Round 4 found one test-integrity issue under the required final red gate; no further fix has started.

